tion":"The correlation matrix for the point-to-point uncertainties for dijet measurements with the $\\textrm{sign}(\\eta_1) = \\textrm{sign}(\\eta_2)$ topology. The $A_{LL}$ uncertainty contribution...","doi":"10.17182/hepdata.104836.v1/t19","id":1034727,"location":"Data from Table 11 in Supplemental Material","messages":false,"name":"Table 11 Supplemental Material","processed_name":"Table11SupplementalMaterial","resources":[]},{"data":{"csv":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 12 Supplemental Material/csv","json":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 12 Supplemental Material/json","root":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 12 Supplemental Material/root","yaml":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 12 Supplemental Material/yaml","yoda":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 12 Supplemental Material/yoda","yoda.h5":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 12 Supplemental Material/yoda.h5","yoda1":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 12 Supplemental Material/yoda1"},"description":"The correlation matrix for the point-to-point uncertainties for dijet measurements with the $\\textrm{sign}(\\eta_1) \\neq \\textrm{sign}(\\eta_2)$ topology. The $A_{LL}$ uncertainty contribution...","doi":"10.17182/hepdata.104836.v1/t20","id":1034728,"location":"Data from Table 12 in Supplemental Material","messages":false,"name":"Table 12 Supplemental Material","processed_name":"Table12SupplementalMaterial","resources":[]},{"data":{"csv":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 13 Supplemental Material/csv","json":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 13 Supplemental Material/json","root":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 13 Supplemental Material/root","yaml":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 13 Supplemental Material/yaml","yoda":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 13 Supplemental Material/yoda","yoda.h5":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 13 Supplemental Material/yoda.h5","yoda1":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/table/ins1850855/Table 13 Supplemental Material/yoda1"},"description":"The correlation matrix for the point-to-point uncertainties coupling dijet measurements with the $\\textrm{sign}(\\eta_1) \\neq \\textrm{sign}(\\eta_2)$ topology and the $\\textrm{sign}(\\eta_1) =...","doi":"10.17182/hepdata.104836.v1/t21","id":1034729,"location":"Data from Table 13 in Supplemental Material","messages":false,"name":"Table 13 Supplemental Material","processed_name":"Table13SupplementalMaterial","resources":[]}],"mode":"record","overall_status":"finished","participant_count":2,"recid":104836,"record":{"abstract":"We report high-precision measurements of the longitudinal double-spin asymmetry, $A_{LL}$, for midrapidity inclusive jet and dijet production in polarized $pp$ collisions at a center-of-mass energy of $\\sqrt{s}=200\\,\\mathrm{GeV}$. The new inclusive jet data are sensitive to the gluon helicity distribution, $\\Delta g(x,Q^2)$, for gluon momentum fractions in the range from $x \\simeq 0.05$ to $x \\simeq 0.5$, while the new dijet data provide further constraints on the $x$ dependence of $\\Delta g(x,Q^2)$. The results are in good agreement with previous measurements at $\\sqrt{s}=200\\,\\mathrm{GeV}$ and with recent theoretical evaluations of prior world data. Our new results have better precision and thus strengthen the evidence that $\\Delta g(x,Q^2)$ is positive for $x > 0.05$.","access_urls":{"links":{"csv":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins1850855/1/csv","json":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins1850855/1/json","root":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins1850855/1/root","yaml":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins1850855/1/yaml","yoda":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins1850855/1/yoda","yoda-h5":"https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins1850855/1/yoda.h5"}},"analyses":[],"arxiv_id":"arXiv:2103.05571","collaborations":["STAR"],"control_number":"104836","creation_date":"2021-03-09","data_abstract":"We report high-precision measurements of the longitudinal double-spin asymmetry, $A_{LL}$, for midrapidity inclusive jet and dijet production in polarized $pp$ collisions at a center-of-mass energy of $\\sqrt{s}=200\\,\\mathrm{GeV}$. The new inclusive jet data are sensitive to the gluon helicity distribution, $\\Delta g(x,Q^2)$, for gluon momentum fractions in the range from $x \\simeq 0.05$ to $x \\simeq 0.5$, while the new dijet data provide further constraints on the $x$ dependence of $\\Delta g(x,Q^2)$. The results are in good agreement with previous measurements at $\\sqrt{s}=200\\,\\mathrm{GeV}$ and with recent theoretical evaluations of prior world data. Our new results have better precision and thus strengthen the evidence that $\\Delta g(x,Q^2)$ is positive for $x &gt; 0.05$.","data_keywords":{"cmenergies":[],"observables":["ASYM","CORR","N"],"reactions":["P P --> JET X","P P --> JET JET X"]},"doc_type":"publication","doi":"10.1103/PhysRevD.103.L091103","first_author":{"affiliation":"American U., Cairo","full_name":"Abdallah, M.S."},"hepdata_doi":"10.17182/hepdata.104836.v1","id":104836,"inspire_id":"1850855","journal_info":"Phys.Rev.D 103 (2021) L091103","keywords":[{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"p p: scattering"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"p p: colliding beams"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"dijet: hadroproduction"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"jet: inclusive production"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"gluon: helicity"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"gluon: momentum"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"p: polarized beam"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"x-dependence"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"polarization: longitudinal"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"spin: asymmetry"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"experimental results"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"200 GeV-cms"}],"last_updated":"Fri, 28 May 